   "source": [
    "STEP 1  - Business Understanding\n",
    "\n",
    "Business Understanding is the first step in the Data Science Lifecycle. In this step, we understand the business problem and decide what we need to predict or solve using data.\n",
    "1. Types of Machine Learning Problems\n",
    "There are two common types of supervised machine learning problems:\n",
    "\n",
    "A. Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "Predicts a category or class.\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "- Email: Spam or Not Spam\n",
    "- Loan: Approved or Rejected\n",
    "- Disease: Positive or Negative\n",
    "- Customer: Will leave or Will stay\n",
    "\n",
    "B. Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "Predicts a continuous numerical value.\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "- Sales prediction: ₹50,000\n",
    "- Salary prediction: ₹40,000\n",
    "- House price prediction: ₹50 lakh\n",
    "- Temperature prediction: 32°C\n",
    "\n",
    "3.How to identify the problem type\n",
    "- If the output is a category or label, use Classification.\n",
    "- If the output is a numerical quantity, use Regression\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, predicting whether a loan will be approved is classification. Predicting the loan amount a customer may qualify for is regression.\n",
    "4. Examples of business understanding\n",
    "Before building a model, define these things:\n",
    "- Problem: What do we want to solve?\n",
    "- Objective: What do we want to predict?\n",
    "- Input features: What information do we have?\n",
    "- Target variable: What do we want the model to predict?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "d7ba78e1-2dc3-4f11-802e-b7bd85d85531",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "STEP 2- Data Acquisition\n",
    "\n",
    "Data Acquisition is the second step in the Data Science Lifecycle. It is the process of collecting data from different sources that we need to solve a business problem.\n",
    "\n",
    "Sources of Data Acquisition\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Files\n",
    "Collect data from CSV, Excel, JSON, and text files.\n",
    "Example: Employee salary data stored in an Excel file.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Databases\n",
    "Collect data using SQL from databases such as MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server.\n",
    "Example: Customer and loan details from a bank database.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. APIs\n",
    "Collect data from applications or online services.\n",
    "Example: Weather data from a weather API.\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Web Scraping\n",
    "Extract permitted information from websites using tools such as BeautifulSoup.\n",
    "Example: Collecting product prices from a website.\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Surveys and Forms\n",
    "Collect information directly from people.\n",
    "Example: Customer feedback and satisfaction ratings"
   ]
  }
